0023:     - Background pixels form 4-connected chambers separated by wall and marker pixels.
0024:     Rule
0025:     - Infer the background as the unique most frequent color and the wall as the unique most frequent remaining color.
0026:     - For each 4-connected background chamber, collect the distinct orthogonally adjacent marker pixels.
0027:     - Recolor that whole chamber to the unique majority marker color, preserving all non-background pixels.
0028:     Key insight
